# add short note on semantics / validation
cat <<'EOF' > pcl/gpu/CUDA12.md
# CUDA 12 / independent thread scheduling

The GPU modules use CUDA texture **objects**, owned by each host invocation.
`TextureView<T>` is a copyable kernel argument; `TextureScope` owns the objects
and keeps them alive through completion on the stream. Linear resources retain
`tex1Dfetch`'s zero-outside-resource behavior, including the NCV filter border
cases. Pitched resources retain the original point/linear filtering, normalized
coordinates, and clamp/mirror addressing. NCV's selected stream is thread-local.
Marching cubes reads its instance's integer lookup tables directly.

Block and warp reductions retain the original addition tree. Shared-memory
stages have explicit barriers and disjoint readers/writers; the ICP and NCV
warp scans/reductions use synchronized register shuffles.

Cloud extraction and marching cubes compact in deterministic column order.
Warps reserve temporary storage independently, record their within-column
positions, and publish column counts. A small exclusive scan and linear scatter
remove scheduling-dependent output ordering. Workspace belongs to each volume
or mesher, and is reused (not global or thread-local). If the caller supplies a
small buffer, extraction regenerates the deterministic prefix using the scanned
column offsets. Triangle writes and returned lengths are bounded by capacity.

## Validation

Configure with `-DCUDA_ARCH_BIN=120 -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=120` (also the
CUDA 12.8 default), `-DBUILD_GPU=ON`, and `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release`.
GPU modules default on when a toolkit is found; they can still be disabled
individually. CUDA 12 no longer disables KinFu, KinFuLS, or people detection.
`cuobjdump --list-elf` and `--list-ptx` should show only `sm_120`.

Run the downstream `kinfu_replay`, `people_eval`, and `ncv_check` without source
changes. Use `OMP_NUM_THREADS=1` for people detection. In addition to normal and
concurrent runs, run each executable under all three of:

```
compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck --error-exitcode 99 ...
compute-sanitizer --tool racecheck --error-exitcode 99 ...
compute-sanitizer --tool synccheck --error-exitcode 99 ...
```

Include volume shifts, repeated mesh/cloud extraction, nonzero NCV seeds, and
multiple people frame variants. Compare poses, packed TSDF slices, point
checksums, labels, and NCV buffers between standalone and concurrent runs.
Time uninstrumented runs separately; racecheck substantially changes timings.
EOF
